   "id": "hook",
   "text": "One f-string, and your whole database is exposed?"
  },
  {
   "id": "bug",
   "text": "Most devs write this."
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "text": "An f-string pastes user input into your SQL, so attackers rewrite the query."
  },
  {
   "id": "fix",
   "text": "Pass the value separately: cur dot execute, percent s, then user id in a tuple. The driver sends data, not code. Injection stopped."
  },
  {
   "id": "bait",
   "text": "Raw parameterized SQL, or an ORM? Comment your answer."
  },
  {
   "id": "follow",
   "text": "Follow K four coding for part four."
